<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Sukō</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1334–<a href="/years/1398">1398</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Sukō was the third emperor of the Northern Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reigning from 1348 to 1351, a son of Emperor Kōgon. He was deposed when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-takauji">Ashikaga Takauji</a> briefly submitted to the Southern Court, and in 1352 Southern forces carried him off with the retired emperors Kōgon and Kōmyō and held him for several years. Excluded from the succession, his line became the Fushimi-no-miya princely house.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-suko.jpg" alt="Emperor Sukō" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 三宅幸太郎 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Suk%C5%8D_by_K%C5%8Dtar%C5%8D_Miyake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
